Headline: THREAT.STO Publish Date: 04/16/1993 .RM288PT/By Jack Burke Staff Reporter

A four-month electronic investigation ended with the arrest of a man 
who allegedly sent terroristic computer messages.

According to University Police reports, John Michael Polzer was 
arrested Wednesday in the act of sending a threatening message to 
Corinne Braun, a University student.

Braun said she began receiving offensive, abusive messages from the 
suspect on her home computer last November.
[...]
Many of the messages came through a program called IRC, or Internet
Relay Chat. The program is available internationally and is often 
used to exchange messages between individuals and groups.
